{"vid":"8rGLrhVeZvw","source":"8rGLrhVeZvw.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":2,"txt":"Shell and tube heat exchangers will look something like this."},{"t":5.8,"txt":"With this design, we normally find the Inlet and the outlet"},{"t":9.5,"txt":"for one fluid at the very end of the heat exchanger known as the header."},{"t":14.5,"txt":"Then we we have another Inlet and outlet"},{"t":16.6,"txt":"for fluid two on the main body known as the shell."},{"t":20.7,"txt":"Inside the unit we have the tubes."},{"t":23.5,"txt":"These bend and loop around to start and finish at the tube plate"},{"t":27.6,"txt":"which sits between the shell and the header."},{"t":30.3,"txt":"The tubes will usually also pass through some baffles, which are sheets of metal."},{"t":36.1,"txt":"We will see how these work in just a moment."},{"t":39,"txt":"The header as well as the tubes can be removed for cleaning, repairs and maintenance."},{"t":44.3,"txt":"Inside the header is a sheet of metal known as the divider or the partition."},{"t":49.5,"txt":"This separates the tube ends,"},{"t":51.4,"txt":"enabling the fluid to flow into and then out of the heat exchanger. Tubes."},{"t":56.4,"txt":"Fluid one will flow through the header, into and around the tubes,"},{"t":61.3,"txt":"then back to the header."},{"t":63.1,"txt":"Fluid two will enter the shell and surround the outside of the tubes."},{"t":68,"txt":"The baffles will partially block the flow"},{"t":70.5,"txt":"which will force the fluid to turn multiple times."},{"t":74.2,"txt":"This creates a turbulent flow and ensures that fluid too mixes with itself"},{"t":80.2,"txt":"which ensures maximum heat transfer."},{"t":82.9,"txt":"For example, we might find this in a pharmaceutical factory"},{"t":87.1,"txt":"with a boiler providing steam into the shell which surrounds the tubes."},{"t":91.7,"txt":"A chemical product is then pumped through the tubes"},{"t":94.9,"txt":"and this absorbs the heat of the steam through the tube wall,"},{"t":98.4,"txt":"so this product is going to exit the heat exchanger much warmer."},{"t":102.7,"txt":"Meanwhile, the steam will start to condense into a liquid"},{"t":106.3,"txt":"and flow back to the boiler to pick up more heat and repeat the cycle."},{"t":110.5,"txt":"Additionally, these are used in refrigeration applications like this industrial chiller."},{"t":116.1,"txt":"We have the water flowing through the tubes"},{"t":118.5,"txt":"and the hot refrigerant in the shell."},{"t":120.6,"txt":"The water will absorb the heat of the refrigerant so that it can transport this to the cooling tower"},{"t":126.7,"txt":"where it will be ejected into the atmosphere."},{"t":129.3,"txt":"The water returns cooler to pick up more unwanted thermal energy from the chiller."},{"t":134.6,"txt":"We have covered how chillers work in great detail previously."},{"t":138.3,"txt":"Do check those out."},{"t":139.2,"txt":"I'll leave a link for you in the video description down below."},{"t":144,"txt":"Double pipe or tube in tube type heat exchanges will look something like this."},{"t":149.9,"txt":"This is similar to the shell and tube heat exchanger"},{"t":153.5,"txt":"because essentially we just have a tube"},{"t":156.3,"txt":"which runs back and forth a number of times between an Inlet and an outlet."},{"t":161.2,"txt":"This is surrounded by a shell which has another Inlet and outlet."},{"t":165.7,"txt":"A metal frame will hold the unit in place."},{"t":168.4,"txt":"Typically, these will all be made from stainless steel."},{"t":171.5,"txt":"One fluid will flow through the tube and another will flow through the shell."},{"t":176.3,"txt":"The two fluids are separated by the tube wall"},{"t":179.4,"txt":"and transfer thermal energy through this tube wall."},{"t":183.4,"txt":"The different configurations result in different temperature profiles and heat transfer."},{"t":188.7,"txt":"In this design, the bend at each end isn't utilised for heat transfer"},{"t":193.7,"txt":"and heat can be wasted here."},{"t":195.5,"txt":"However, manufacturing this heat exchanger is cheaper and obviously easier."},{"t":200.4,"txt":"Other designs like this hairpin type heat exchanger"},{"t":203.9,"txt":"which are often found in oil refineries"},{"t":206.7,"txt":"will encapsulate the bend to fully utilise the surface area for heat transfer."},{"t":212.4,"txt":"This version normally uses multiple tubes to maximise the surface area"},{"t":217.5,"txt":"and thus increase the heat transfer"},{"t":220,"txt":"although this will also increase the resistance."},{"t":223,"txt":"These are a fairly simple heat exchanger design and are very common"},{"t":227.4,"txt":"particularly in food processing as well as pharmaceutical production."},{"t":232.3,"txt":"For example, we might have a dairy product flowing through the tube"},{"t":236.6,"txt":"and then we have hot water or maybe even steam flowing in the opposite direction through the shell"},{"t":242.5,"txt":"which will warm the product up to a certain temperature"},{"t":246,"txt":"before it is mixed with some other ingredients and then bottled."},{"t":250.6,"txt":"Check out one of these videos"},{"t":252.3,"txt":"to continue learning about mechanical and thermal engineering"},{"t":255.8,"txt":"as this is the end of the video, don't forget to follow us on Facebook LinkedIn Twitter."},{"t":261.1,"txt":"Instagram tiktok as well as Theengineeringmindset.com."}],"words":[{"t":2,"w":"Shell"},{"t":2,"w":"and"},{"t":2,"w":"tube"},{"t":2,"w":"heat"},{"t":2,"w":"exchangers"},{"t":2,"w":"will"},{"t":2,"w":"look"},{"t":2,"w":"something"},{"t":2,"w":"like"},{"t":2,"w":"this."},{"t":5.81,"w":"With"},{"t":5.81,"w":"this"},{"t":5.81,"w":"design,"},{"t":5.81,"w":"we"},{"t":5.81,"w":"normally"},{"t":5.81,"w":"find"},{"t":5.81,"w":"the"},{"t":5.81,"w":"Inlet"},{"t":5.81,"w":"and"},{"t":5.81,"w":"the"},{"t":5.81,"w":"outlet"},{"t":9.49,"w":"for"},{"t":9.49,"w":"one"},{"t":9.49,"w":"fluid"},{"t":9.49,"w":"at"},{"t":9.49,"w":"the"},{"t":9.49,"w":"very"},{"t":9.49,"w":"end